            "review_text": "SaigonExile\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam166 contributions\n0\nTypical Problem in Viet Nam\nJan 2018 • Solo\nFirst of all, let me say I love shopping here! It's the 'go to' place for good and hard to find products. The selections are eclectic and reasonably priced for what you get.\n\nWhat I hate is, and every shop, store, place of business in Viet Nam is guilty of this; \n\nCashier: Do you have a membership card.\nCustomer: No, I don't.\n\nAnd the conservation ends there. No attempt whatsoever to close a sale. I would take a membership card if only the employees showed any interest in offering one. Does anyone at all train their employees to make an offer and then attempt to close the sale? In my 10 years here the answer is 'no'.\n\nPlease train your employees. Oh, and when 14 people are in line please open the other register. You don't need two employees at one register. I can bag myself if necessary. \n\nOther than this, a great shop!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 24, 2018",
